 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 9,
   "y": 1,
   "plaque": "arts_norwich_school",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "The Norwich School",
   "text": "In 1803 a weaver's son called John Crome founded the Norwich Society of Artists, the first art movement in Britain to grow up outside London. Crome and John Sell Cotman painted the Norfolk they could walk to: heaths, wherries, windmills and big skies, with a looseness that was ahead of its time. The castle keeps the largest collection of their work. Cotman's watercolours are kept out of the light, which is what he did to the sky."
  }
